; Low from a pair. Winning 42 p. 49 (S-0071-c); the 84 form p. 70
; (S-0097-c); played in Hand 35 (S-0151-e, S-0151-h).
; Rule, in our words: a setter following a suit, whoever led it, in which he
; holds exactly two tiles, neither of them count, plays the lower and keeps the
; higher. Against a bid of marks, where count no longer matters and every
; trick does, he keeps two tiles of the suit of the bidder's double to the end:
; he plays the lower on the double, count or not, and keeps the higher for the
; off.
; Replaces gates/c13c-low-from-a-pair.silas. How it differs: the first rule is
; the gate's (the book's leader is anyone, as the gate already reads it). The
; 84 form is new: the gate needs a pair without count, so it is silent where
; the book plays low from a pair that holds a count tile.
; The book against its rule: in Hand 29 trick 3 (S-0133-j) the right setter
; holds the 6-1 and the 3-1 on his partner's 1-0; the book says either will
; do and plays the higher, the 6-1, as he has another six. The rule allows
; only the 3-1 there.

(include book)

(policy low-from-a-pair
  (rule follow-low (play low)
    (roles me low high led)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (led-context led)
    (not (trump led))
    (follower low)
    (count low 0)
    (follower high)
    (count high 0)
    (beats high low led)
    (none (roles third) (follower third) (not (tile third low)) (not (tile third high))))
  (rule keep-the-higher-for-the-off (play low)
    (roles me doubled low high led)
    (viewer me)
    (setter me)
    (every-trick)
    (bidder-led doubled)
    (double doubled)
    (led-context led)
    (not (trump led))
    (follower low)
    (follower high)
    (beats high low led)
    (none (roles third) (follower third) (not (tile third low)) (not (tile third high)))))
